1. skills/do-work/tools/do-work-cli/internal/gittransaction/git_transaction.go (+9/-4)
   a. quarantineAndRollbackPrivate (HEAD line 1204): first statement, before the privateTransactionTestHook call, becomes
      if root == nil {
          // The rollback open failed and rollbackFailure kept going so every other target is
          // still unstaged and reported. Nothing rooted can run here: the published bytes stay
          // where they were published, and the report names the target and the missing handle,
          // the same answer rollbackDirtyTracked gives for the same condition.
          return "", fmt.Errorf("rollback root is unavailable; private target left as published: %s", state.path)
      }
      Placed inside the consumer, not at the call site, because the function has two callers (rollbackFailure:1032 unguarded, rollbackDirtyTracked:1189 guarded) and the dereference at root.Mkdir (1213) belongs to the function; the guard now travels with the dereference. The error names the target on purpose: rollbackDirtyTracked's sibling message is the bare "rollback root is unavailable", which cannot be attributed when several targets are declared. Both call sites already consume ("", err) by appending err.Error() to rollback.Errors and continuing (rollbackFailure:1033-1036 and :1017-1020), so no call-site edit and no silent skip.
